destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4665192daf88749bedffff255b59ecfb81018f0d674610f05b3e9381b040346d","title":"Which adopted quantum-gravity restrictions obstruct detectable vacuum-generated primordial gravitational waves? The source reviews a steep-potential criterion and TCC, then invokes a refined curvature branch to accommodate a small first slow-roll parameter.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:46d2f275bb7b71b49beec5631d1ed2d092ac470fd32a2701f3a89ab4539a54e6","title":"Can one low-energy principle identify theories excluded by forced extra gauge factors, invalid geometric tunings and extra rational sections? The obstacle is that anomaly and string-charge data specify a homology class without visibly specifying the distinguished gauge-supporting curve.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:46fdbb1003d0cb8c25a4c56b529ea26ee11ff0982d6012790950705feff0b8ea","title":"How do effects non-perturbative in α′ resolve the formally negative conformal factor near negative D3 charge, and can KKLT stabilization and uplift remain reliable when the affected region occupies an O(1) fraction of the compactification?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0061"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4634c4e0f5badeb68f72c0046dec48829430215a08b0c43b93c29c71f960bb49","title":"The Joyce resolution allows bulk-radius KK towers to be compared with exceptional wrapped-M2 particles while distinguishing seven untwisted and 36 twisted periods.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:464b08b6201ce086f0769d74260c6a8e315cf80261d793fbb7e9140fc48b1e8d","title":"How do chiral anomalies obstruct circle lifts of odd-dimensional theories, and can five-dimensional BPS-string unitarity constrain six-dimensional supergravity and elliptic Calabi–Yau geometry?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:469ee4501419e395c32c25d65527c8c8b0b2626fbdce9ffe36f32f9429fcb07f","title":"Do cosmological parameter discrepancies indicate new physics, statistical fluctuations, analysis approximations or unmodelled systematics? This Snowmass review identifies theoretical, observational and statistical opportunities for distinguishing these possibilities.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4611629e523e1578d8f58984a29a57cfcfd16f8e0ce4a912bb029dc4168e74db","title":"What categorical symmetry results from gauging finite groups and split finite 2-groups in three dimensions, including topological surfaces, Wilson lines, condensation defects and their junctions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:46946e525fe39390e5628700be546e66ce32d703950412b98250bd2b38e0deb8","title":"Can a controlled string compactification reproduce both the Starobinsky scalar potential and its fixed conformal coupling to matter fermions, rather than only an observationally similar inflationary plateau?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0081"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:46c41950d53989562dbf9dda9108cd22d5ab3a757acc354a8a672e78b7372d54","title":"Can a universe realized by thin-wall bubble nucleation during decay of a nonsupersymmetric AdS vacuum have a finite maximum radiation temperature and minimum size, and can string flux parameters and inflationary observations constrain those quantities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0086"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{